WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.600
I just found out like two minutes ago that Lorraine Warren, the author of the cases

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.560
that some of these Conjuring movies are based on,

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:07.860
has just passed away.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:11.880
So I'm gonna go ahead and dedicate this episode of Things You Missed to Lorraine Warren.

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:16.139
If you want to hear about how La Llorona sets
up for another movie, then stick around to

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:17.540
the end of this video.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:23.199
Welcome back to Things You Missed.

00:00:23.199 --> 00:00:24.449
But first, rant time.

00:00:24.449 --> 00:00:28.650
I know it's become kind of a horror cliche
for a character to brush off something supernatural

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:33.000
by telling themself it was just in their imagination,
but The Curse of La Llorona takes this to

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.660
the most ridiculous level I've ever seen.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:40.680
Like almost every character has ample opportunity
to say, "Hey, that thing that just happened.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:41.680
That wasn't normal.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:42.680
Maybe I should get help.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:45.640
Maybe I should make like Andre 3000 and get
up and go to church."

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:46.640
But they don't.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:47.710
It's so frustrating.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:51.409
Like those two Alvarez boys who tell the social
worker that, "she'll hurt us" if they leave

00:00:51.409 --> 00:00:52.409
the closet.

00:00:52.409 --> 00:00:56.140
Why would you say that and not clarify that
you're talking about a spooky ghost and not

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:58.190
their mother who's being investigated?

00:00:58.190 --> 00:00:59.790
And then the main family is even worse.

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:03.739
They each have individual encounters with
La Llorona, and when asked what happened,

00:01:03.739 --> 00:01:05.869
they're like, "no, nothing happened."

00:01:05.869 --> 00:01:10.100
The Mom, I get, she has to uphold her credibility
because she has a job.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:14.350
But the kids have no reason to hide it, and
it’s just completely illogical.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:18.150
And then, around the midpoint, they all encounter
La Llorona together, and then they basically

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:21.540
get together and decide, "Nope, that was nothing
right?

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:23.540
We didn't see anything."

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:27.070
But anyway, that was frustrating, let's move
onto the Things You Missed.

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:31.049
The first clue that this is just the Conjuring
but with Spanish legends, comes as soon as

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:34.230
we get into the main setting of the movie,
Los Angeles 1973.

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:38.720
A long, fast-moving handheld tracking shot
takes us through the house in the exact same

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:40.900
style of the opening of The Conjuring.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:44.159
When we first meet Anna's daughter Sam, she's
watching an episode of Scooby Doo.

00:01:44.159 --> 00:01:48.119
This is probably the point where everyone
leaves a comment about me being Shaggy's brother,

00:01:48.119 --> 00:01:53.140
so I'm only gonna use 0.1% of my power to
extract this Thing You Missed.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:57.470
The episode she is watching features someone
pretending to be a ghost in order to terrorize

00:01:57.470 --> 00:01:59.860
people, as many Scooby Doo episodes do.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:03.690
At the end of The Curse of La Llorona, we
are led to believe, however obvious it may

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:08.239
have been, that La Llorona broke the fire
seed barrier setup at the door and got into

00:02:08.239 --> 00:02:12.480
the house, when in reality, it was actually
Patricia Alvarez, the mother who had her two

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:17.370
sons taken by La Llorona, and thought by sacrificing
Anna's kids, she could get hers back.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:21.340
She wears similar clothing and takes off her
shoes to give her the appearance of the ghost,

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.719
just like the villain in that Scooby Doo episode.

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:27.600
The actress who plays Anna also played Velma
in the live action Scooby Doo movies.

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:31.959
The scene where Samantha sees La Llorona through
the clear umbrella next to the swimming pool

00:02:31.959 --> 00:02:36.310
is very reminiscent of a short film called
Cam Closer, in which the supernatural occurrences

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:38.219
only show up through a cell phone camera.

00:02:38.219 --> 00:02:42.319
I’d like to believe that the umbrella scene
isn’t blatant plagiarism, because the director

00:02:42.319 --> 00:02:47.590
of Cam Closer, David F Sandberg, also directed
Annabelle Creation, which is a part of this

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:50.499
universe, so maybe they had his blessing to
lift the concept.

00:02:50.499 --> 00:02:54.459
I’d still love to see Cam Closer adapted
into a feature film in the style of Lights

00:02:54.459 --> 00:02:55.459
Out.

00:02:55.459 --> 00:02:58.909
But speaking of the lights being out, and
yes, I’m aware that was a terrible transition,

00:02:58.909 --> 00:03:02.730
during the scene that takes place in the middle
of the night where Anna calls out asking if

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:06.200
someone is in the house… as if the intruder
or ghost is just going to be like “oh you

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.200
got me, April Fools!”

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:11.240
But as Anna goes back into her room, if you
look to the right side of the doorway, you

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:14.980
can spot La Llorona just standing there in
the corner, hiding in the dark.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:18.760
Now I was going to point out that Father Perez
is the same priest that helps out Mia and

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:22.239
John in Annabelle, but the movie makes it
pretty clear when he explains that he opened

00:03:22.239 --> 00:03:25.950
his mind to things out of the ordinary after
an incident with a doll, so I'll point out

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:28.430
a couple of other Annabelle connections instead.

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:32.219
Misty is the name of the doll that Sam carries
around, and nearly kills them all when she

00:03:32.219 --> 00:03:36.269
accidentally breaks the fire seed barrier
when trying to grab the doll from outside.

00:03:36.269 --> 00:03:40.299
It resembles a Raggedy Ann doll, the real
life version upon which the Annabelle doll

00:03:40.299 --> 00:03:41.439
is based on.

00:03:41.439 --> 00:03:45.409
Also, in my last episode when I talked about
the Annabelle Comes Home trailer, one of the

00:03:45.409 --> 00:03:49.030
things I pointed out was this wedding dress
in the Warren’s room of cursed objects.

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:52.870
Now that La Llorona is confirmed to be part
of The Conjuring universe, I think it's very

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:55.409
likely that this is La Llorona's dress.

00:03:55.409 --> 00:03:59.829
Anna is, afterall, able to collect the sapphire
locket off while trying to banish her from

00:03:59.829 --> 00:04:03.440
the house, so it stands to reason that by
fully defeating the weeping woman, Ed and

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:05.799
Lorraine Warren could at some point obtain
this dress.

00:04:05.799 --> 00:04:09.650
It is hinted that she survives at the end
of the movie, based on the final shot where

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:13.049
Anna looks back and sees something in the
reflection of the puddle, which is consistent

00:04:13.049 --> 00:04:17.079
with numerous occasions of La Llorona appearing
in mirrors and causing them to break.

00:04:17.079 --> 00:04:20.160
But does this mean we are going to see La
Llorona Dos?

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:21.850
Well I have a better suggestion.

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:25.860
The Conjuring and The Conjuring 2 both open
with Ed and Lorraine Warren on a case that’s

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:27.800
unrelated to the main case of the movie.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:31.820
The director of The Curse of La Llorona was
Michael Chaves who is also supposed to direct

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:33.070
The Conjuring 3.

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:36.600
Father Perez tells Anna that the church has
people who can deal with evil spirits, but

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:39.150
it takes several weeks for these things to
be approved by the church.

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:43.190
We see the same thing happen in The Conjuring,
where the exorcism isn’t approved until

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:44.620
after it’s already over.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:53.360
"The vatican approved the exorcism."

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:55.800
"Hm. Nice timing."

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:00.140
So my idea is that Father Perez puts in the
request for Anna anyways, and the opening

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:04.950
of The Conjuring 3, or really any Conjuring
movie, shows La Llorona being defeated, her

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:08.730
spirit being locked inside of the wedding
dress which is kept safely in Ed Warren’s

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:09.730
home.

00:05:09.730 --> 00:05:13.180
As far as further connections go, the Shaman
Rafael who helps out the family explains he

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:16.600
no longer works with the church and he made
it seem like there’s some history there

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:20.120
-- so I wouldn’t be too surprised to see
more of his story in another movie.

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:23.770
This next one is a bit of a spoiler if you
haven’t seen The Conjuring 2, but I think

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:25.180
we all kind of know what happens.

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:28.990
When they finally do banish La Llorona by
stabbing her with the cross, she disappears

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:32.990
in a manner that looks almost exactly like
the defeat of Valak at the end of The Conjuring

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:37.180
2 where Lorraine banishes the demon back to
hell, so it seems possible that neither one

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:38.990
of these entities is gone for good.

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:42.710
I’m gonna be doing a little mini marathon
where I’ll be covering all thee Annabelle

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:48.120
movies here on Things You Missed, so remember
to subscribe to CZsWorld for new horrors every

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:52.560
week, ring the deathbell for notifications
and I’ll see you in the next one.

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:55.080
Assuming we both survive.

